{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 30, "timestamp": 1787301753, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "env": {"SHELL": "/usr/bin/zsh", "TERM": ""}, "title": "M4: the CodePipeline engine"}
[0.007847, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 1. Where this recording came from\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.511755, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# Provenance first: branch, short commit, and whether the tree was clean.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.515527, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.520868, "o", "v3\r\n\u001b[1;32m$ git rev-parse --short HEAD\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.526235, "o", "a68cad8\r\n\u001b[0;90m# An empty listing means a clean tree.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[7.530005, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ git status --porcelain | grep -v \"^ M .claude\" | head\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.540525, "o", "?? docs/proof/m4-pipeline.cast\r\n"]
[8.540999, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 2. Zero wrapper code in the user's app\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.04517, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The whole M4 opt-in is one config file. No import of the wrapper in bin/, no CDK Pipelines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[12.049167, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# constructs -- the app stays exactly what 'cdk init' produced.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[14.052959, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ sed -n \"1,14p\" test/fixtures/pipeline-app/cdk.json test/fixtures/pipeline-app/bin/app.ts\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[15.059477, "o", "{\r\n  \"app\": \"npx cdk-cicd exec bin/app.ts\",\r\n  \"output\": \"cdk.out\"\r\n}\r\n#!/usr/bin/env node\r\n// The application the m4 pipeline deploys. Deliberately trivial -- one SSM parameter -- so the gate\r\n// asserts \"the pipeline really deployed this stage's stack\" without any app-specific machinery. The\r\n// stack is `cdkcicdtest-<run-id>-app`, distinct from the `cdkcicdtest-<run-id>-pipeline` stack that\r\n// deploy-ci provisions, and both carry the cdkcicdtest- prefix the teardown guard requires.\r\n//\r\n// The run id comes from the bundle's run.json, NOT the environment -- see lib/run-id.ts for why.\r\nimport * as cdk from 'aws-cdk-lib';\r\nimport { runId } from '../lib/run-id';\r\nimport { PipelineFixtureStack } from '../lib/stack';\r\n"]
[15.059528, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ cdk.json points at 'cdk-cicd exec'; the app itself is a plain CDK app.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[17.063337, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 3. One flat pipeline, rendered from that config\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[18.567434, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# The engine turns the config into a single CodePipeline. Source, a CI Build, a self-updating\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[20.571508, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# stage that re-deploys the pipeline from config each run, then ONE deploy action per stage.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[22.575905, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# A non-dev stage is gated: a manual approval is ordered ahead of its deploy.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[24.579512, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node test/proof/demos/lib/m4-pipeline-tour.js default\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[26.092595, "o", "Pipeline stages (each box is a stage; -> is run order):\r\n\r\n  Source          Source [Source/S3]\r\n  Build           Build [Build/CodeBuild]\r\n  UpdatePipeline  SelfMutate [Build/CodeBuild]\r\n  dev             Deploy-dev [Build/CodeBuild]\r\n  prod            Approve-prod [Approval/Manual]  ->  Deploy-prod [Build/CodeBuild]\r\n"]
[26.092694, "o", "\r\nFootprint: 4 CodeBuild project(s)\r\n           v2 (CDK Pipelines) grew one project per asset per stage -- 100+ on a real app.\r\n"]
[26.116784, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ 4 CodeBuild projects total -- 1 CI, 1 self-update, 1 per stage. v2 grew 100+.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[28.120362, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 4. The prod gate is fail-closed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[29.624217, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# prod's approval runs at run-order 1 and its deploy at 2, so the deploy cannot start until a\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[31.628004, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# human approves. Rejection or the 7-day timeout fails the stage -- nothing ships unapproved.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[33.631667, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 5. Opt-in: hand the CloudFormation wait to a Lambda\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[35.135688, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# With asyncDeploy the deploy stage stops paying build compute to watch CloudFormation: the\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[37.1408, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# build prepares change sets and exits, and a small stateful Lambda executes and awaits them.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.144686, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$ node test/proof/demos/lib/m4-pipeline-tour.js async\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[40.704327, "o", "Pipeline stages (each box is a stage; -> is run order):\r\n\r\n"]
[40.704386, "o", "  Source          Source [Source/S3]\r\n  Build           Build [Build/CodeBuild]\r\n  UpdatePipeline  SelfMutate [Build/CodeBuild]\r\n  dev             Deploy-dev [Build/CodeBuild]  ->  Await-dev [Invoke/Lambda]\r\n"]
[40.704721, "o", "  prod            Approve-prod [Approval/Manual]  ->  Deploy-prod [Build/CodeBuild]  ->  Await-prod [Invoke/Lambda]\r\n\r\nFootprint: 4 CodeBuild project(s), 2 deploy-driver Lambda(s)\r\n           v2 (CDK Pipelines) grew one project per asset per stage -- 100+ on a real app.\r\n"]
[40.715127, "o", "\u001b[1;33m→ Off by default -- the build-compute path above is what m4-verify proves end to end.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[42.71884, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m 6. Proven on real AWS\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[44.22347, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# This shape is not just rendered -- test/proof/m4-verify.sh provisions it from a bare config on\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[46.227462, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# the test account, flows a commit dev -> prod through the manual approval (driving the gate with\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[48.23209, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# codepipeline put-approval-result), asserts both stage stacks, then tears everything down.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[50.235865, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# It has PASSED end to end in the default assembly-promotion model on the test account; every AWS\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[52.240182, "o", "\u001b[0;90m# call there is redacted, so no account id leaks into this recording.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[54.244269, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36mM4: one config, zero wrapper code in the app, one flat pipeline with gates and self-update -- where v2 grew 100+ projects.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
